    kfree(hostcmd);
    return -ENOMEM;
}
```
```c
if (err) {
    kfree(hostcmd);
    kfree_skb(skb);
    return -EMSGSIZE;
}
```
Reason:
These statements ensure that the allocated memory for `hostcmd` is freed in all error handling paths before the function exits, thus preventing memory leaks. The `kfree(hostcmd)` calls are added to release the memory when an error occurs, ensuring proper memory management.

